# A range as a value (notes/layers.md, sugar): `a to b` (also `a … b`) is the list of the ints from a through b, `a..b`
# the same without b, each end computed once. A loop over a range counts without the list (core/extensions/sugar/iteration.warp), and the
# rest of a list pattern, `rest...`, has no end. A range of whole numbers holds only its two ends (decision
# lazy-range-value, runtime/lists.warp range_value): count, #, sum and r#i answer from them, any other list word makes
# its items
rewrite $a to $b => range_value($a, $b) where $a is int and $b is not missing
rewrite $a .. $b => range_value($a, $b - 1) where $a is int and $b is not missing
rewrite $a to $b => ($xs = ø; $i = $a; $end = $b; while $i <= $end { $xs += [$i]; $i++ }; $xs) where $a is not missing and $b is not missing
rewrite $a .. $b => ($xs = ø; $i = $a; $end = $b; while $i < $end { $xs += [$i]; $i++ }; $xs) where $a is not missing and $b is not missing
